As a rather messy workaround, the following can be done:
/**
* Implements hook_ENTITY_TYPE_presave().
*/
function my_module_media_presave(\Drupal\Core\Entity\EntityInterface $entity) {
/** @var \Drupal\media\Entity\Media $entity */
$entity->thumbnail->alt = $entity->field_media_image->alt;
}
Another slightly less messy workaround may be to implement a bundle class wrapping Media entity, and extend preSave function to force updateThumbnail from there, like this:
<?php
namespace Drupal\my_module\Entity;
use Drupal\Core\Entity\EntityStorageInterface;
use Drupal\media\Entity\Media;
/**
* A bundle image class for media entities.
*/
class MediaImage extends Media {
/**
* {@inheritdoc}
*/
public function preSave(EntityStorageInterface $storage) {
parent::preSave($storage);
$this->updateThumbnail();
}
}
I hope this can help someone in the meantime.

